{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch","id":1463829,"title":"New W5 info from the 14th of October Twitch","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-14T08:27:33-07:00","id":1463829,"title":"New W5 info from the 14th of October Twitch","content":"So a prerecorded interview with Justin Achilli is going on right now on the <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/worldofdarkness\" target=\"_blank\">worldofdarkness twich channel</a><br /> <br /> They've moved onto Hunter now, but I thought people who don't have the time to watch everything will be interested in the following:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Two native american cultural advisors on the team<br /> Tribes as less tied to geography and culture and more to concept<br /> Focus on younger werewolves trying to reclaim what was lost<br /> World is fucked up horribly but not post apocalyptic<br /> Umbra as a hostile place, caerns cut off from the spirit world<br /> haglust (spelling?) -&gt; opposite to Harano, hysterical zeal, embodied by a new antagonist tribe that may or may not be right<br /> Focus on renown as something that empowers the Garou<br /> Getting rid of Metis and Pure Breed<br /> No more Garou Shall not Mate with Garou </div> </div> </div>I'll add anything else if they loop back to Werewolf later on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 10-14-2021, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T08:30:47-07:00","id":1463831,"title":"","content":"Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T08:50:23-07:00","id":1463834,"title":"","content":"Don't know how they're going to pass some of that through without some heavy retcons. Also, continued boo on clamping down on Umbra instead of focus on chulorviah going further inland due to sea level rise from climate change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T09:05:33-07:00","id":1463837,"title":"","content":"Dino, I know that you and I would probably really enjoy playing in the same game, but they continued by doubling down later in the stream &quot;Umbra is actively rejecting the werewolves&quot;. This screams Avatar Storm 2.0 and everything that came along with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T09:12:30-07:00","id":1463839,"title":"","content":"Okay, it sounded good until the Umbra thing (urgh.) As for the metis, I need to be honest they were going to be cut anyway. Metis as a concept is rife with ableism and child abuse, stuff that no longer flies as easily as it did when 1e was released.<br /> <br /> The removal of Garou shall not Mate with Garou, though, makes me a bit worried. In Forsaken, that made sense, since uratha are very much a disperate people. But garou are more structured.<br /> <br /> Has there been anything about the lupus breed?<br /> <br /> In general, it sounds like Forsaken a bit too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T09:14:00-07:00","id":1463840,"title":"","content":"Nothing was said about Lupus or breed at all. Only that the &quot;Metis are out&quot;. From my point Umbra and the spirits were one of the strongest points of Werewolf and I can quite agree with misgivings towards that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T09:30:07-07:00","id":1463843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the metis, pure breed and breeding changes are good but this comes with caveats. Namely, instead of saying this sounds like Forsaken(and to note I am a big CofD fan) the way I'd put it is more that it's taking the lessons learned from Forsaken. However this is not all positive for me because with the increasing use of that with the book approval situation etc I am increasingly distrustful of Paradox and it's plans for CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When I say it is too much like Forsaken, I mean it is losing elements that make Forsaken and Apocalypse different games. If we lose lupus, friendly umbra, garou having to seek mates outside the Nation, etc. the game-lines are starting to become a BIT too similar in ways that aren't helpful.<br /> <br /> For example, one thing in Forsaken that I think would be good would be the loss of the Curse. It is crystal clear for me that most writers and players REALLY want to have their characters hold regular jobs. Which is near impossible in core WtA. That is a change that would be long term helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T10:17:46-07:00","id":1463848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's less I'm saying you're wrong on that assessment and more I think the motivation has far more to do with looking at why design decisions were made and going, &quot;Yeah that is a good idea.&quot; Even as someone who is extremely cautious right now about Paradox I don't think the changes are for sus reasons. So It's not really about making the games similar as it is about utilizing good ideas. Also I cannot emphasize enough to anyone in the thread not familiar with Forsaken, the cosmologies of WoD and CofD are so vastly different that I'd say saying the games are becoming more similar is surface level at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the changes are for sus reasons, I can totally see why they went where they went.<br /> <br /> But I would say the changes are not surface level even with different cosmologies. The umbra for the garou is a lifeline, it is extremely important to the whole garou society that they have safe access to the umbra. The concept of Caerns relies on the umbra being something friendly. If the umbra is hostile, then the trips to it are very close to how uratha deal with them. As in, high risk.<br /> <br /> Just that change alone makes the game play extremely differently from typical WtA.<br /> <br /> My worry is that what made both Forsaken and WtA stand out from one is taken away. Garou are blessed, they are chosen, they are the warriors of Gaia with a global society. Uratha are eking out a living in small groups and everything hates them. W5 has the garou be hated by the umbra, the young garou trying to reclaim past glory and their society not having the need to breed with humans/wolves anymore.<br /> <br /> When WoD20th was released, it benefitted from the CofD mentality of not being so strict with world building. It could throw new ideas in without changing the core of the games. W5 feels more like trying to take the elements of Forsaken that made it be its own game and transplant them to WtA. And while some are things that needed to change (tribe names, metis,etc.) some are actively removing elements that WtA relies on.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T11:28:17-07:00","id":1463862,"title":"","content":"Ultimately we don't have enough information to know how surface level these changes are going to be.<br /> <br /> The Umbra isn't exactly friendly in WtA already. It's supposed to be a dangerous place. The Penumbra is full of unfriendly spirits; esp. in cities. The Realms all follow strange rules based on what they represent. Moonbridges can get attacked by raiding spirits. Etc. Highlighting this a bit more might feel more surface level like Forsaken, but it wouldn't really be a meaningful change.<br /> <br /> However, the Garou have an ancient pact with Gaian and &quot;neutral&quot; spirits that means there's a whole section of spirits they have a default good relation with. The Umbra around a Caern is so friendly because the Garou do a lot of work to cultivate Caerns as places where the spirits most friendly to them are dominant. If the line about Caerns being less connected to the spirit world (whatever that means... Caerns are literally a place were there's a hole in the wall between worlds) means that pact is gone, and the Gaian spirits are now hostile to Garou that don't stick to the flesh world... that's a very deep change, and one towards Forsaken since it means even &quot;friendly&quot; spirit dealings get more brutal than mystical.<br /> <br /> The only thing that's undeniably good is the first point in the list. Everything else comes with massive caveats regarding execution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T11:35:50-07:00","id":1463863,"title":"","content":"Zeal tribe? Children of Gaia I bet. For me it's all disappointing. Like wrong turn. I feel like someone hammered my head. with some heavy thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T11:49:27-07:00","id":1463866,"title":"","content":"One of the reasons given for &quot;Garou shall not mate with garou&quot; and the fact that it predates the birth if the first metis, was that Gaia/Luna/prehistoric Garou (or whoever came up with the Litany tenets) thought that if the garou would procreate with each other they would loose focus on their human and wolf relatives. And, while I find it okay, that Metis are gone as a concept, I would like to seem them replaces by a &quot;garou won't get children from sex with other garou&quot; - and make sexual contact between garou and human/wolf not obsolete...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T11:54:36-07:00","id":1463867,"title":"","content":"First Ronin was first metis. What with Perfect metis. They would burry the myths and legends of game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T12:03:39-07:00","id":1463868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1463862#post1463862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that's undeniably good is the first point in the list. Everything else comes with massive caveats regarding execution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah pretty much. The Tribes being overhauled to be tied to specific geographic areas and real world cultures is fine and I honestly think is something long overdue. For some Tribes it never really mattered but others had the annoying trait of demanding PCs be of a certain ethnic group or from a certain area.<br /> <br /> But everything else is at best questionable until we see how it is executed and at worst, a massive retcon of a long existing setting for questionable reasons.<br /> <br /> Years ago I had a high school friend was Metis and we did play some WtA. He wasn't crazy about the name for two reasons. First it's the exact opposite of what the name Metis meant and just didn't make sense to him (or me for that matter). And second, he didn't like the vaguely incestous undertones of the breed in Garou society sharing the name of his people. Which yeah, I can see how bad that would look. But all that required was a simple name change of the Breed. I don't think anyone would complain if they completely retconned the Metis breed name to a fake name.<br /> <br /> But getting rid of the Breed or more specific the deformities and infertility of them is a bad idea as if the Garou can breed with each other just fine, why do they need humans? Why didn't they just wipe them out eons ago? And why would Garou society interact with Human society if they don't need humans to continue their own race? Why wouldn't most of Garou society be living as those off the grid survivalist types out in the wilderness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T12:14:08-07:00","id":1463869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1463867#post1463867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First Ronin was first metis. What with Perfect metis. They would burry the myths and legends of game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if the retcon Metis out of the game. If they say, there haven't been new Metis born since the year 2000 or so, the Metis would be removed as a PC option and that is okay.<br /> If the go the &quot;Children of Osiris&quot; way - and each metis is turned into a homid or lupus breed by Luna, because she is crazy, that's fine, too....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T12:15:30-07:00","id":1463870,"title":"","content":"That would be blessing for every metis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T12:19:10-07:00","id":1463871,"title":"","content":"Beyond the name change, there's lots of options for the Garou-born (hell, that phrase is already something to use instead!) that get rid of the issues. The Kitsune, for example, go in largely the opposite direction. The Shinju aren't stigmatized, if anything the opposite, but each of their parents has a 50/50 chance of dying from it. Plenty of a good reason to not just have Kitsune mate with other Kitsune on that alone. Most of the Fera are either incapable of making a changer-changer baby (ex: Corax), or have a far less problematic place in their culture for them. It's not like the concept is beyond repair.<br /> <br /> Fixing it is still going to be a major retcon in some fashion, but I can't see it being less disruptive than just taking them completely out of the game (and Litany).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T14:05:09-07:00","id":1463882,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Two native american cultural advisors on the team- </b></i><br /> This is good....now whether they listen and implement anything they say is another thing.<br /> <i><b>Tribes as less tied to geography and culture and more to concept</b></i><br /> This is a tightrope, by Revised the only tribe still tied to 'one' culture was Little Brother, all the rest had some historical roots in certain cultures but were spread far and wide across the world.<br /> <i><b>Focus on younger werewolves trying to reclaim what was lost</b></i><br /> <br /> So basically WtA then?<br /> <i><b>World is fucked up horribly but not post apocalyptic</b></i><br /> <br /> Looking out the window this is true.....but I have a feeling in this context this means an excess of edge and very little meat.<br /> <b><i>Umbra as a hostile place, caerns cut off from the spirit world</i></b><br /> <br /> Fuck off! The Umbra was already plenty hostile.....we do not need Avatar Storm/Hisil bullshit.<br /> <b><i>haglust (spelling?) -&gt; opposite to Harano, hysterical zeal, embodied by a new antagonist tribe that may or may not be right</i></b><br /> <br /> Another metamorphic plague but emotional? Cos that sucked the first 3 times it was mentioned.....but now it applies to all Garou, I nominate this as the rule everyone forgets was in the book.<br /> <i><b>Focus on renown as something that empowers the Garou</b></i><br /> <br /> ? Ok.....uneccessary change for uneccessary change sake but ok....kinda leans a little hard on meritocracy for my taste but fine. People recognising your deeds makes you spiritually stronger?<br /> <br /> <i><b>Getting rid of Metis and Pure Breed</b></i><br /> <br /> Not too fussed though for fucks sake make it a retcon and not some convuluted metaplot bullshit. I've had some great Crinos-Born characters over the years but I can see why. Pure Breed can just be renamed to better fit what it actually represents in terms of Patron recognition.<br /> <br /> <i><b>No more Garou Shall not Mate with Garou</b><br /> <br /> This will also need to be a retcon and the impact on what Garou society looks like will need to be examined properly.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T15:36:50-07:00","id":1463891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1463866#post1463866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the reasons given for &amp;quot;Garou shall not mate with garou&amp;quot; and the fact that it predates the birth if the first metis, was that Gaia/Luna/prehistoric Garou (or whoever came up with the Litany tenets) thought that if the garou would procreate with each other they would loose focus on their human and wolf relatives. And, while I find it okay, that Metis are gone as a concept, I would like to seem them replaces by a &amp;quot;garou won't get children from sex with other garou&amp;quot; - and make sexual contact between garou and human/wolf not obsolete...</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, why even have kinfolk at this point? If we lose kinfolk most of Garou society breaks down as kinfolk are more numerous, work jobs to support the Garou, insert themselves into human society to try to help the Gaian cause, and are there to remind the Garou what is worth fighting for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T19:50:04-07:00","id":1463935,"title":"","content":"I could actually see the Garou not always being with other Garou in relationships, because the phrase &quot;you can't help who you fall in love with&quot; can cut in a number of ways; some of them are just going to want to be with otherwise normal humans or wolves, or humans or wolves born to other Garou, simply because they ended up meeting and clicking. Besides, the Nagah manage to keep kin lines even when they can be with each other without consequence, with a blessed Nagah-born (ahi) happening only once in a mother's lifetime and all other children being of the mother's breed.<br /> <br /> But some packs are likely to become more like wolf packs, particularly where the Red Talons are concerned. I mean, assuming that they didn't get booted for being hard cases and all. If it's a retcon, that may be the prior core of Garou society. Would go a long way toward educating readers about how wolves actually are, if nothing else.<br /> <br /> Pure Breed thoughts: This one is kind of a bit of egg on my face, I don't know if anyone else feels that way. PB should have been renamed Heroic Lineage in W20. I'm feeling rather dumb for not having advocated for that, since I was there pulling for changes about ten years ago when it was being written. Seems like it would have been an easy change, but perhaps I just forgot where my head was at the time.<br /> <br /> Renown: It already got into the effects of more Gifts than it probably should have in W20, especially ones that served as duplicated effects for Fera that don't even have the same Renown types. Not sure why it would need even more emphasis when Boli Zousizhe can use high Honor/Virtue (presumably) scores to body anyone who attacks their family or pack with Fu Xi's Honor (duplicated for the Warding Mokole in the form of Rage of the Nest Mother, which is coincidentally in the list for Zhong Long warriors).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T01:39:53-07:00","id":1463982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1463891#post1463891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly, why even have kinfolk at this point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because W20 Kinfolk granted them more magic. They are the thin-blooded of the Garou. They might not be able to put disciplines into flasks, but maybe they can soon put Gifts into small medicine bag like tokens....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T01:44:25-07:00","id":1463983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1463935#post1463935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could actually see the Garou not always being with other Garou in relationships, because the phrase &quot;you can't help who you fall in love with&quot; can cut in a number of ways;</div> </div> </div> </div>But a statistically relevant number of people find their partner in the workplace. And, unless it gets removes from the game entirely, there is the Curse.<br /> <br /> Sure, today, garou can fall for a human, force them to have sex with the Animal Magnetism mechanic, and get satisfied for a while. But the Curse should prohibit this from being something that lasts. So, garou-garou relationships are the only one's that make sense, and they were the permanent friend-zone in the past, but not anymore...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T03:41:25-07:00","id":1463995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1463982#post1463982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because W20 Kinfolk granted them more magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? While K:ABA added some Rites that kin can learn and do (though are explicitly not empowered by the spirits unless a Garou gets involved), giving Kin default access to Numina was a thing back in Unsung Heroes as well. So this feels like a weird claim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T04:52:23-07:00","id":1464004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1463995#post1463995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh? While K:ABA added some Rites that kin can learn and do (though are explicitly not empowered by the spirits unless a Garou gets involved), giving Kin default access to Numina was a thing back in Unsung Heroes as well. So this feels like a weird claim.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also had kinfolk variants of tribal Gifts and in general to tone and general outlook of the passages I read (which were those dealing with the Gifts primarily) seemed to indicate that powers of these kinds were supposed to be more common among Kinfolk, than it was in Unsung Heroes. Could be my interpretation of what I read, but if W20 had a statement like &quot;Roger Delay is an Athro and has about 15 or so Gifts, imagine what a Kinfolk would need to accomplish to get one. Never think about a second.&quot; then I missed it. Instead of some original Kinfolk Gifts with powers that, in my opinion, made sense, they went the modified tribal Gift way - which was recycling for some parts. Kind of annoying, given the fact that authors often complain about word count restrictions...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T05:59:42-07:00","id":1464016,"title":"","content":"I've always felt that one of the core themes of Werewolf was family.<ul><li>The found family - the pack, the totem</li> <li>The family by blood - someone that may have fathered you in a tryst, a family group that you don't gel with or the caring family that knows your darkest secret</li> <li>The spirits that have followed your family and that your family has followed through their lives, and the strange and infinitely complex world that reaffirms and proves your Faith</li> <li>The ancestors themselves who are literal embodiment of legend and justification of living a &quot;good&quot; Garou life</li> <li>The responsibility and expectations of your extended family - kinfolk or the tribe</li> <li>Living up to the legend and renown of the parents you have never met and whose legend is death or the fact that they don't see you as good enough or maybe even you don't see them as good enough?</li> <li>Living up to the legend of your parentage and being judged for their actions and choices while trying to make your own</li> </ul><br /> It's a strange interaction of Pure Breed, Ancestors and Renown, but it's actually something that enriched Werewolf and created a lot of quality storytelling. Pure Breed as it stands is not really required, but a larger interaction of who came before you and whose deeds you need to live up to or atone for is something that's deeply ingrained into Werewolf. Heroic Lineage could work here quite well.<br /> <br /> Outside that the whole disconnection of the tribes from the real-world cultures seems a bit reactionary and based on a lot of the early missteps and decisions made in early Werewolf. Revised and W20 made great strides to represent how the Tribes are so much more than the cultures that inspired them, how they exist all over the world and have long blended with many cultures and societies. I can see there being a need to sand down the rough points further and working on the Pure Tribes, but actually dropping the geographical and ethnographic distinctions will do them no favors. One of the best things that Werewolf has taught me is that Shifters adapt to the local culture and that I should learn more about the world, its history and its culture to make things work.<br /> <br /> However, I don't feel that this is something nuWW is into. A lot of their choices seem to exist for either simplicity or cheap thrills, without actually exploring the consequences of their choices on the world. A world where the young are separated from the old, where there is no legacy to protect or overcome, and where the spirit world is no longer a part of who you are is not the kind of Werewolf that draws me in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T06:09:35-07:00","id":1464018,"title":"","content":"Very, very well said, Asmodai. I think you hit the nail right on the head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T11:08:07-07:00","id":1464055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1463983#post1463983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But a statistically relevant number of people find their partner in the workplace. And, unless it gets removes from the game entirely, there is the Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither of these rule out Kin. The default status of every caern is &quot;doesn't have enough Garou to get everything done&quot;, so a number of Kin are likely going to be helping out in some capacity under Garou supervision. Kin are also unaffected by the Curse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, today, garou can fall for a human, force them to have sex with the Animal Magnetism mechanic, and get satisfied for a while. </div> </div> </div>Not even remotely what I was going for. Also, I hope that Animal Magnetism gets reduced and simplified into adding PU to seduction and partying rolls, because having a whole system for it seem extra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the Curse should prohibit this from being something that lasts. So, garou-garou relationships are the only one's that make sense, and they were the permanent friend-zone in the past, but not anymore... </div> </div> </div>The Curse only kicks in if Rage is higher than the human's Willpower, and there could conceivably be ways around even that, if you dump enough into social traits.<br /> <br /> Besides, between Garou being sparse and various dimensions of pack, sept, and tribe politics, getting hitched to another werewolf could come with a lot of baggage that would make some hesitate to go through with it. Marrying into the Shadow Lords in particular is liable to ensure that your life is perpetually complicated, and gets more and more complicated each passing day. Proudly proclaiming that you're with one of the Bone Gnawer rabble is courageous and heartfelt, but could also cost support from snooty septs of mostly other tribes. There's a pretty interesting new territory to navigate there, as long as you don't immediately dismiss the concept as &quot;yiff in hell!&quot;, because even with the first tenet out of the way and no auto-disabled Garou-Garou kids, it's not going to be a simple matter. Just cross your fingers and hope that the Black Furies don't become Werewolf Drow.<br /> <br /> Response to Other Posts, Topic Change:<br /> <br /> As to the removal of metis as a whole, they've had the opportunity to do interesting things with it, and make insightful commentary. But they also mostly end up as props to show how bad Garou are, and there may need to be a subtler approach to showing how messed up Garou society is, which doesn't involve authors of splatbooks making dad jokes about the similarity in spelling between the breed and an ethnic group in Canada (see the 2nd edition Silver Fangs TB for that one), or the Thrall of the Wyrm turning a character into a sex criminal just 'cause. And if you ask, &quot;Hey, Saur, aren't you disabled/chronically ill from birth? Do you want to keep the option to explore that open?&quot; the only thing I can say is that I'm rather tired with that dimension of W:tA, and don't want to have to live through being dismissed for trying to explain the difference between my existence and others' more than once. Once was honestly alienating enough.<br /> <br /> (I never had a thyroid, for reference.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T15:37:14-07:00","id":1464097,"title":"","content":"Also.... removing them doesn't remove the option to play Garou with disabilities or even supernatural deformities. There are Flaws for those already. We don't need disabilities attached to a Breed to be able to explore them if we want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T15:39:43-07:00","id":1464098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464055#post1464055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither of these rule out Kin. The default status of every caern is &quot;doesn't have enough Garou to get everything done&quot;, so a number of Kin are likely going to be helping out in some capacity under Garou supervision. Kin are also unaffected by the Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW, they are less affected by the Curse, which is kind of not saying anything, since the mechanics of the Curse are somewhat totally up to the Storyteller. And while statistically 1 or 2 out of 10 people a garou tries to walk by on the side walk should just turn around an run away screaming, it never happened in any game I was a player in.<br /> <br /> 2nd Edition had a game mechanic, rolling every month if some event happened that destroyed the garou's attempt at a normal/human life. It should, imo, never have been removed from the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464055#post1464055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Curse only kicks in if Rage is higher than the human's Willpower, and there could conceivably be ways around even that, if you dump enough into social traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... maybe. I could see a system, where you can use a social roll, possibly something with performance, to downplay your Rage and for a scene get by without the Curse foiling your social life. But besides that, there are only Gifts/Fetishes that help and frankly, they shouldn't be common. The Curse in one great dilemma for the Garou and it has taken a back seat in most games, imo.<br /> <br /> Also, if the Metis are removed from the Setting, shouldn't the 100% Garou offspring chance also be removed?<br /> There is no need for that anymore. If Garou/human and Garou/kinfolk parings without Pure Breed (that is going away, too) are at 10%, why not make the chance of garou/garou kinds being garou 20% or throw in a bonus to make it 50%....<br /> <br /> I wonder, if without Pure Breed, the chances of breeding true will increase just because more people know I'm a powerful garou. So bonus by Renown. Then, a true born kind gives Renown. Full Circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T09:23:55-07:00","id":1464259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464098#post1464098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW, they are less affected by the Curse, which is kind of not saying anything, since the mechanics of the Curse are somewhat totally up to the Storyteller. And while statistically 1 or 2 out of 10 people a garou tries to walk by on the side walk should just turn around an run away screaming, it never happened in any game I was a player in.<br /> <br /> 2nd Edition had a game mechanic, rolling every month if some event happened that destroyed the garou's attempt at a normal/human life. It should, imo, never have been removed from the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>It never should have been in the rules, because one roll saying &quot;oh, you fucked up, and are now a drifter&quot; is far less nuance or play than one typically wants for upheaval of a character's status quo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well... maybe. I could see a system, where you can use a social roll, possibly something with performance, to downplay your Rage and for a scene get by without the Curse foiling your social life. But besides that, there are only Gifts/Fetishes that help and frankly, they shouldn't be common. The Curse in one great dilemma for the Garou and it has taken a back seat in most games, imo. </div> </div> </div>Everything needs rethinking or revisiting at some point. Since the Curse is so wishy-washy, it might not exist in its present form by the time W5 lands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if the Metis are removed from the Setting, shouldn't the 100% Garou offspring chance also be removed? </div> </div> </div>I'd generally assume that they're handling it more like 3E Dragon-Blooded is handling the chances for a character's offspring to be Dragon-Blooded. That'd make it a good chance if both parents are Garou, but not a certainty. Kinfolk, following the example of folks with DB ancestry who aren't themselves Terrestrial Exalted, would only reduce the chances slightly when with one Garou, and they still have a decent chance compared to past models with two Kin. It would only be when kin/non-kin pairings come into play that it would drop significantly.<br /> <br /> Of course, that would hold true for the Dancers as well, though the dimensions of their children not being inherently mutated shock troops would mean a significant change to how lineages and sexual politics work in the tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T10:32:09-07:00","id":1464267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1463843#post1463843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> When I say it is too much like Forsaken, I mean it is losing elements that make Forsaken and Apocalypse different games. If we lose lupus, friendly umbra, garou having to seek mates outside the Nation, etc. the game-lines are starting to become a BIT too similar in ways that aren't helpful.<br /> <br /> For example, one thing in Forsaken that I think would be good would be the loss of the Curse. It is crystal clear for me that most writers and players REALLY want to have their characters hold regular jobs. Which is near impossible in core WtA. That is a change that would be long term helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>So...this is actually how a lot of people feel about Masquerade and Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T11:05:57-07:00","id":1464269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464267#post1464267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So...this is actually how a lot of people feel about Masquerade and Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>The new V5 or V20?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T12:18:01-07:00","id":1464275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464259#post1464259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It never should have been in the rules, because one roll saying &quot;oh, you fucked up, and are now a drifter&quot; is far less nuance or play than one typically wants for upheaval of a character's status quo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. It was a single roll, but that was only the indicator to the ST to build an event into the unfolding story that (partly) destroys the garou's place in the human world, if the character had build some place for him. The PC in question could still do something and mitigate the fallout.<br /> <br /> And, I found it good, because it wasn't so whishy-washy but was a clear indicator, should the ST get active or let it move on as a non-topic for yet another downtime....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T17:35:10-07:00","id":1464291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464269#post1464269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new V5 or V20?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire 5th edition (V5)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T17:43:14-07:00","id":1464292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464275#post1464275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. It was a single roll, but that was only the indicator to the ST to build an event into the unfolding story that (partly) destroys the garou's place in the human world, if the character had build some place for him. The PC in question could still do something and mitigate the fallout.<br /> <br /> And, I found it good, because it wasn't so whishy-washy but was a clear indicator, should the ST get active or let it move on as a non-topic for yet another downtime....</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually, you should take more care before letting an established setting and character relationships blow up, especially in a system this much of a stickler for detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T18:57:00-07:00","id":1464299,"title":"","content":"Caveats about anecdotes and so on:<br /> <br /> I know a ton of WtA groups that dropped that rule while playing 2e. I know one that brought it back in Rev. or W20. The one ST that I know that did that doesn't have a group that lets him run games any more, because he actually expanded that rule, and made the consequences worse, and nobody felt like playing with him because they don't want to have a 1/10 chance of retiring a character at the start of every session because random badness happened between scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T23:20:09-07:00","id":1464317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464291#post1464291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampire 5th edition (V5)</div> </div> </div> </div>It does seem like the books are bridging the gaps between oWoD and nWoD a lot. If I were to guess, maybe Paradox doesn't want two very similar game settings running parallel, thus the push for oWoD games to take on nWoD traits. Maybe in hopes of combining the oWoD and nWoD versions at some point?<br /> <br /> Though, this is just a guess.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T02:10:11-07:00","id":1464336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464317#post1464317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does seem like the books are bridging the gaps between oWoD and nWoD a lot. If I were to guess, maybe Paradox doesn't want two very similar game settings running parallel, thus the push for oWoD games to take on nWoD traits. Maybe in hopes of combining the oWoD and nWoD versions at some point?<br /> <br /> Though, this is just a guess.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My guess is they want to profit of the wod name but would rather be producing cod style work.<br /> It all come across as cynical and will probably hurt both in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T04:01:29-07:00","id":1464354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Two native american cultural advisors on the team </div> </div> </div>A good first step. I'm somewhat sceptical; is two enough, will they have bias, did they have to work through a bunch of advisors before they could get someone to agree with them...?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tribes as less tied to geography and culture and more to concept </div> </div> </div> so long as it's &quot;less tied&quot; and not &quot;<i>we removed geographical and cultural influences</i>&quot;. Werewolf is about tribalism after all, Tribes aren't your myers-briggs/Hogwarts House/university, they're tribes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Focus on younger werewolves trying to reclaim what was lost </div> </div> </div>Ok, sure, that doesn't really mean anything to me, I mean it could, but so could a politician saying he wants to save the children, it could mean anything or nothing. I prefer my werewolves raging against the dying of the light, but I'm not entirely opposed to &quot;reclaim what was lost&quot; even though that sounds loaded with imagined pasts...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> World is fucked up horribly but not post apocalyptic </div> </div> </div>Status quo. Nice.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Umbra as a hostile place, caerns cut off from the spirit world </div> </div> </div>Erm. If Caerns are cut off from the spirit world, how the fuck are they still Caerns? Shit idea. Denies options. You could almost quantify this change as objectively bad.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> haglust (spelling?) -&gt; opposite to Harano, hysterical zeal, embodied by a new antagonist tribe that may or may not be right </div> </div> </div>Haglust sounds like werewolves in first edition. I like it. A new antagonist tribe? Eh... I mean, if it's a new antagonist tribe (or the skin dancers) then I'm all for the idea. If you want to make my beloved [insert tribe here] a bad guy faction, you can fuck right off.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Focus on renown as something that empowers the Garou </div> </div> </div>Intriguing. How is there any difference from before. Genuinely curious. This could be cool.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Getting rid of Metis and Pure Breed<br /> No more Garou Shall not Mate with Garou </div> </div> </div>Fuck off. This is just stupid. Garou aren't heroes, they're people with power, radicalized monsters with heroic traits and delusions of granduer. They're meant to be deeply flawed, and &quot;garou shall not mate with garou&quot; is an important mythic trait. Like Irish legends struggling with Geas or greek legends struggling with prophecies and fate, McBeth needing a lawyer to deal with witches. Yes, the word metis is insensitive shit too close to reality and needs to be changed, but complicated relationships, themes of shame, forbidden love and traumatic childhoods? That's storytelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-18-2021, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T05:07:56-07:00","id":1464356,"title":"","content":"Haglust has taken one of the existing tribes. They are playing coy about who it is. They say that there are only 11 tribes now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T05:20:52-07:00","id":1464361,"title":"","content":"My guess would be Red Talons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25975-queenherla","name":"QueenHerla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25975_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T05:25:48-07:00","id":1464362,"title":"","content":"Interesting, looking at Heart of the Forest it seems like Get to me. Then again, that's assuming they're all on the same page which is probably a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T08:38:06-07:00","id":1464385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464299#post1464299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caveats about anecdotes and so on:<br /> I know a ton of WtA groups that dropped that rule while playing 2e. I know one that brought it back in Rev. or W20. The one ST that I know that did that doesn't have a group that lets him run games any more, because he actually expanded that rule, and made the consequences worse, and nobody felt like playing with him because they don't want to have a 1/10 chance of retiring a character at the start of every session because random badness happened between scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the rule was misinterpreted then. Let's see the rules:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the Storyteller's option, every character who is attempting to live a human life can be required to make a Willpower roll between each story; the difficulty is the Rage score of that character. If the roll fails, something has happened to ruin or hinder the character's relationship with the people among whom he has been living. The Beast has emerged, the Delirium has engaged, and never again shall the character be trusted. This penalty may be lessened should the character be so fortunate as to have Kinfolk.<br /> A botch indicates that not only has the character lost control, but agents of the Wyrm have discovered her whereabouts and may be in the process of an attack. The player and Storyteller should immediately go into roleplaying mode and deal with this issue. </div> </div> </div>The text in the DriveThru version isn't manually corrected OCR, so there might be spelling mistakes above...<br /> <br /> So, last sentence indicates, we are not in roleplaying mode when this happens. Not that the book tells of &quot;modes&quot; a lot. But I guess &quot;roleplaying mode&quot; is a scene, while elements not in a scene but in a story are downtime, according to page 206 of 2nd Ed core rules. Elements between stories are are also downtime I guess, interludes in the chronicle - paraphrasing page 52-55 of 2nd Edition Core rules.<br /> <br /> Roll is Willpower against Rage. So, WP 10 against Rage 10 has a 31% percent failure rate. But, next to every human runs away in panic anyway, so the garou wouldn't have had time to build a relationship with humans, right?<br /> Let's see WP 8 Rage 6 -&gt; slightly under 8% failure chance. So, not so drastic....<br /> <br /> But what even happens with a failure?<br /> &quot;...something has happened to ruin <b>or hinder</b> the character's relationship with the people among whom he has been living...&quot;<br /> So, no need for character retiring at all. I mean, ruin relationships with humans or hinder them? That can totally be a lot of things.<br /> Question is, what was the character trying to have as a &quot;human life&quot;? Is it family, job or both?<br /> What ever the case, something happened that made his Rage come to the surface and therefore lowered the difficulty of some Empathy roll so that one or more humans felt a glimpse of the garou's true self and it backfired.<br /> <br /> Found a job as bank teller? Great, until that one day, you got frustrated with poor old hard-of-hearing Mrs. Walters. It was just your expression that you couldn't control for a moment and she realised something. Next Monday, no senior citizen stood in line at your counter and when the last of month came, you were let go.<br /> <br /> Had a family? Great, until that one fight you had with your wife. Your grabbed the bowl full of hot soup, ready to hurl it at her. You didn't, but little Tommy saw. He is afraid, your wife is afraid, you are afraid yourself. Nothing to bad happened, but the bond of trust is shattered. It's best to move out, maybe only temporary. Trust need to be rebuild. You can't force that.<br /> <br /> The rules don't say something about Frenzy, Carnage, Murder, Veil-lifting, Deaths or wounding or any of the things that destroy a character. They tell about destroying (or hindering) things the garou had been building <b>that resemble a &quot;normal&quot; human life</b>.<br /> <br /> There is also not stated, the ST should dictate terms, or prohibit these Downtime events lead into scenes. On the contrary, page 206 describes that Downtime Play can and should develop into a scene organically. So, build scenes around how the character reacts after the fight with this wife, or how he feels alone in the motel that night, or couch surfing at his packmates later that week. Does the character use Persuation to keep his job as bank teller, possibly settle with the bank manager to transfer to another branch after a short sabbatical?<br /> Also, the ST should work with the Players, as described in the Storys section of the Rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> A lot of topics in these forums have several users stating, that they don't see garou holding an every day job or human life, because of the Curse, and also peer pressure as mandated by possible renown loss for not being garou full time. But it was 2nd Edition &quot;Family Tragedy&quot; mechanics that made this Setting Element an actual game element, instead of a mere Setting description. And that is, why it should be back in W5 and be used (in a way that enriches the game).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 10-18-2021, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T09:24:30-07:00","id":1464386,"title":"","content":"My money on the Fenris as the unplayable tribe or playable as some kind of not-problematic option.<br /> Shitty idea, no, seriously, what the fuck.<br /> Every damn tribe has some kind of problem, a tragedy, a fucked up thing that comes as crash between tradition and progress, some kind of abusive or aggressive thing that comes from the possible extremization of the tribe's way of life. <br /> That's the <b>NICE THING</b> about werewolf the apocalypse: tragedy, and to face seriously bad shit, abuse, racism, and other stuff that comes from tribal society. This is supposed to be an adult game, a mature game, I don't wanna play the world of darkness according to some kind of moral. I want to play it because <b>IT IS</b> made up by injustice, tragedy, and shit. I have had many people around my table, of many kind, ethnic group, disabled persons and so on, and all of them wanted to face this kind of shit through werewolf. Damn. I would say they also found a way to express their anger or their thoughts about social justice and modern day problems thanks to werewolf. It was a chance to face those things. To be the hero, to take vengeance, to <b>let your anger go without consequences</b>, because it is game, to think about consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T10:38:39-07:00","id":1464392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464354#post1464354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is just stupid. Garou aren't heroes, they're people with power, radicalized monsters with heroic traits and delusions of granduer. They're meant to be deeply flawed, and &quot;garou shall not mate with garou&quot; is an important mythic trait. Like Irish legends struggling with Geas or greek legends struggling with prophecies and fate, McBeth needing a lawyer to deal with witches. Yes, the word metis is insensitive shit too close to reality and needs to be changed, but complicated relationships, themes of shame, forbidden love and traumatic childhoods? That's storytelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>(We've actually been told that Garou are a type of hero, in a number of places, of a &quot;keep struggling to the end to give everything a fighting chance&quot; type.)<br /> <br /> Tragic loves in myth rarely have the same baggage as Garou-born, you can come up with a sad backstory from any tale of the First Change and alienation from wolves or humans, and the monstrous side of the Garou is plainly evident in how the consequences of the collective actions of the Garou still haunt them. Presumably, the Wars of Rage are still in, as is the Impergium and concomitant Delirium. Hell, whoever was trying to write for the metaplot kept trying to steer Garou into &quot;we're getting the Impergium back on!&quot; even though they have no more power or means to really do that anymore unless some other force is holding human scrutiny back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T12:24:37-07:00","id":1464401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464392#post1464392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (We've actually been told that Garou are a type of hero, in a number of places, of a &amp;quot;keep struggling to the end to give everything a fighting chance&amp;quot; type.)<br /> <br /> Tragic loves in myth rarely have the same baggage as Garou-born, you can come up with a sad backstory from any tale of the First Change and alienation from wolves or humans, and the monstrous side of the Garou is plainly evident in how the consequences of the collective actions of the Garou still haunt them. Presumably, the Wars of Rage are still in, as is the Impergium and concomitant Delirium. Hell, whoever was trying to write for the metaplot kept trying to steer Garou into &amp;quot;we're getting the Impergium back on!&amp;quot; even though they have no more power or means to really do that anymore unless some other force is holding human scrutiny back.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't follow your argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T12:54:28-07:00","id":1464407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464385#post1464385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the rule was misinterpreted then.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, as I said, the one ST in question made the rules and consequences harsher. He didn't misinterpreted them, he thought they were too lenient, and house ruled them to be worse for the PC.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T19:48:24-07:00","id":1464452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464401#post1464401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't follow your argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take away Garou-born, and you still have thoroughly monstrous Garou; moreover, the math on their survival up to the present becomes a bit less miraculous. However, you also shouldn't discount their heroic potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T20:39:43-07:00","id":1464456,"title":"","content":"I'm getting Mage Revised vibes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T20:41:18-07:00","id":1464457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464386#post1464386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My money on the Fenris as the unplayable tribe or playable as some kind of not-problematic option.<br /> Shitty idea, no, seriously, what the fuck.<br /> Every damn tribe has some kind of problem, a tragedy, a fucked up thing that comes as crash between tradition and progress, some kind of abusive or aggressive thing that comes from the possible extremization of the tribe's way of life.<br /> That's the <b>NICE THING</b> about werewolf the apocalypse: tragedy, and to face seriously bad shit, abuse, racism, and other stuff that comes from tribal society. This is supposed to be an adult game, a mature game, I don't wanna play the world of darkness according to some kind of moral. I want to play it because <b>IT IS</b> made up by injustice, tragedy, and shit. I have had many people around my table, of many kind, ethnic group, disabled persons and so on, and all of them wanted to face this kind of shit through werewolf. Damn. I would say they also found a way to express their anger or their thoughts about social justice and modern day problems thanks to werewolf. It was a chance to face those things. To be the hero, to take vengeance, to <b>let your anger go without consequences</b>, because it is game, to think about consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll take that bet. You can join the Get of Fenris in the Heart of the Forest game. If you do, she basically says, &quot;What the fuck guys. My ancestors were the Polish resistance and you act like they were Nazis. Fuck you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T23:15:36-07:00","id":1464463,"title":"","content":"So, these are my first impressions...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Two native american cultural advisors on the team. </div> </div> </div>Great! And I hope they don't just provide advice on the Native American tribes, but also on Animism as a whole. It'd be awesome to have more details on how the Garou deal with nature spirits on a day-to-day basis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tribes as less tied to geography and culture and more to concept. </div> </div> </div>Interesting, as long as the Tribes don't become the clubs they are on Forsaken. Your Tribe is your heritage, you don't get to freely choose it, you belong to it even before your birth and to renounce your birthright has grave consequences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Focus on younger werewolves trying to reclaim what was lost. </div> </div> </div>That's fine, I like small scale stories. Forsaken already did this and it worked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> World is fucked up horribly but not post apocalyptic. </div> </div> </div>I wonder how much fucked up it will be. Big climate changes may have huge impacts on some populations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Umbra as a hostile place, caerns cut off from the spirit world. </div> </div> </div>Umbra as a hostile place was already done on Forsaken, do we really need to copy it? Why? I like the idea that the Umbra can be a dangerous place if you don't know what you are doing, but I also like the idea that the Spirit World can be beautiful and feel even more alive than the Material World. Why change it?<br /> <br /> Caerns cut off from the Spirit World??? So the whole idea of having holy places where the Garou can gather and that the Garou must protect will be simply thrown away. This seems stupid in so many ways I can't even begin to describe it. The Garou culture, their existence as One People, revolves around the Caren. Kill this and what do they have left? I like to tell stories of warriors fighting to protect their sacred lands, I don't want to be forced to only tell stories of warriors that lost their territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Haglust (spelling?) -&gt; Opposite to Harano, hysterical zeal, embodied by a new antagonist tribe that may or may not be right. </div> </div> </div>Very interesting! I really liked this idea! See? MORE options is good, LESS options is bad! Also I'll bet the Red Talons had enough and brought the Impergium back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Focus on renown as something that empowers the Garou. </div> </div> </div>This may be interesting, but the Garou are already &quot;powered&quot; by Rage, Gnosis and Willpower. I'd like to see more on this topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Getting rid of Metis and Pure Breed. </div> </div> </div>Getting rid of the name &quot;Metis&quot; I can understand, but I see no reason to get rid of the Breed. Again, MORE options is good, LESS options is bad! The Metis are not just werewolves with deformities, they represent much more than that and they offer a huge number of roleplay opportunities. It seems someone is really trying to turn Apocalypse into Forsaken.<br /> <br /> And Pure Breed makes total sense from a Garou perspective. This is another unnecessary change and these changes are becoming annoying. I surely can houserule this Background back, and I will, but if I have to houserule too many things I may decide it's easier to stick with W20. I'm VERY satisfied with the game as is and I don't NEED another edition. I'd love to continue supporting the line, like I've been doing since the first edition, but I won't buy any more books if they decide to turn Apocalypse into Forsaken-wannabe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No more Garou Shall not Mate with Garou. </div> </div> </div>Oh, come on!!! Give Werewolf: the Apocalypse back to someone that actually LIKES this game! Good times when we had Bill Bridges and Ethan Skemp...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img19/986/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":2766,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2766-wolfen","user":"Wolfen","date":". 10-19-2021, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2766-wolfen","name":"Wolfen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2766_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T23:43:41-07:00","id":1464466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464407#post1464407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, as I said, the one ST in question made the rules and consequences harsher. He didn't misinterpreted them, he thought they were too lenient, and house ruled them to be worse for the PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that defeated the purpose then....<br /> <br /> Should have made clearer, that I was responding to this statement, too...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464292#post1464292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usually, you should take more care before letting an established setting and character relationships blow up, especially in a system this much of a stickler for detail.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T23:46:19-07:00","id":1464467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464457#post1464457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'll take that bet. You can join the Get of Fenris in the Heart of the Forest game. If you do, she basically says, &quot;What the fuck guys. My ancestors were the Polish resistance and you act like they were Nazis. Fuck you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't. <br /> <br /> I'm gonna say it and I don't care if people will not understand: I want some of the get of fenris in my chronicles ALSO to be' some kind of fascist. Yes. I said it. I don't even care. <br /> What do we expect from a might is right tribe which is seeying her mother dying and every way they tried to save her , failing? We seriously expect to see them, all of them, moderate and not problematic? Oh come one. <br /> Ethnic tension, social tension, rampant pollution, global warming. This game is supposed to be' adult. We got genocidal red talons, terrorist Bond gnawers, abusive fianna, and vaguely fascist fenris is offensive ? Why ? Where is the maturity here ?<br /> I despise the nazi. A lot. And I despise the fascists. That doesnt mean that removing a realistic faction of the get will solve my problem with them. White wolf took distance from this shit many times. But this is an adult game, always has been, and basically every person I know like it because with every tribe comes some kind of problem within their tribal nature. Every tribe has some kind of internal internal conflict. Progress vs tradition. When they refuse to embrace adaptation they fail. When they forget or forsake tradition, they lost themselves. When they radicalize themselves, something bad happen. <br /> To have a well done and well depicted Extreme faction is not a way to exclude people or to offend someone. On the countrary, its a good way to face, to truly face problems. Fenris ways, even if moderate can be' seen as fascist in many ways. <br /> A character who is raised by an aryan brotherhood like pack and now sees the truth on the world, rediming himself , a story of deep redemption and pain.<br /> A character who is the grandson of an ss soldier and now is facing mistrust by other garou just because his bloodline. <br /> A bigot fenrir who is saved by a non binary garou or a masculinity-speecher who is in fact gay. <br /> I only see interesting stories coming out from the Extreme faction of every tribe. I see complications. I see very human antagonists and even very tragic protagonists in stories of redemption and sacrifice. <br /> <br /> Nobody wants fascist gamers at their table. But I want stories to tell. Rough, dirty, dangerous stories and honestly I dont fear to be' judged because of my creativity and my Players ability to Play a mature game where mature stuff happens, where dangerous characters can pop up.<br /> I like my werewolf game problematic and ambiguous when it comes to morality, justice, nature , anger , hate, war and social justice. <br /> To force player to Play fascist character or to say &quot;this tribe is fascist&quot; would be' of course extremely unjust, attract wrong people at the table and so on. And I'm not saying this. <br /> And I'm not against a moderate offshot. Im against the removal of an important tribe, the one that makes you think the most about that part of anger and solutions that bring you straight to intolerance. My feeling here is that the tribe would be' removed not because it's a fascist tribe (which is not) but just because the fenris have &quot;porblematic &quot; point of views. Which is just stupid and immature. <br /> <br /> But better to have the fenris removed than totally warped I suppose. Sadly.<br /> Pure Marketing ? Probably .<br /> I hope this message is clear enough because people seems to like to misunderstand this kind of things just to feel morally superior. <br /> <br /> Sorry for my poor english.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 10-19-2021, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T00:27:20-07:00","id":1464472,"title":"","content":"I think they'll get rid of the GoF because that's such a <i>them </i>thing to do. <br /> <br /> The thing is, realistically, if you had a breakaway faction, I don't think it'd be so clear cut as to take away a single tribe. This is likely a human issue, not a spirit one. I'd much rather see factions of the GoF, RT, BG,SL, W,U, F, BF... basically anyone who wants to get radicalized will join the new extremist group. That'd 1: be more realistic and 2: Add some diversity and intrigue to the new faction and 3: would serve to add options rather than take them away because you're not screwing any one tribe in particular, you're just offering something that players can take or leave. <br /> <br /> Clearly, if you were thinking of the good of the game for everyone, you'd be going for that plan. If you're thinking of just cutting out problematic players, you'd just get rid of a tribe. It's clear where they stand. And with an attitude like that, you can expect nothing good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T00:30:42-07:00","id":1464473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464472#post1464472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they'll get rid of the GoF because that's such a <i>them </i>thing to do. <br /> <br /> The thing is, realistically, if you had a breakaway faction, I don't think it'd be so clear cut as to take away a single tribe. This is likely a human issue, not a spirit one. I'd much rather see factions of the GoF, RT, BG,SL, W,U, F, BF... basically anyone who wants to get radicalized will join the new extremist group. That'd 1: be more realistic and 2: Add some diversity and intrigue to the new faction and 3: would serve to add options rather than take them away because you're not screwing any one tribe in particular, you're just offering something that players can take or leave. <br /> <br /> Clearly, if you were thinking of the good of the game for everyone, you'd be going for that plan. If you're thinking of just cutting out problematic players, you'd just get rid of a tribe. It's clear where they stand. And with an attitude like that, you can expect nothing good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you on everything , like I always do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T00:36:24-07:00","id":1464474,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s like I\u2019ve been telling people. The bad in the world of darkness is not there for you to emulate it. Gaia gave you claws and rage to fix it. You, the player, are supposed to do the heroic thing. <br /> <br /> People are worried about offending players. There\u2019s some cases where I can understand that. The Unihar of forsaken was an exceptionally brutal concept, the reasoning for that removal made sense. But at the same time some of this stuff that people are crying for, removal of kinfolk as an example, why? And if you know the person at your table has issues with that type of content why are you subjecting them to it? <br /> <br /> There\u2019s a responsibility on the story teller to know where the line is with your players. We could just as easily have games where the Metis aren\u2019t constantly abused as we could go full fianna hatred. The choice was always in our hands. No one had a gun to our heads saying we needed to subject our players to it. <br /> <br /> Glass half full, I think w5 is going to be a good game. If the fenrir are out though, I\u2019m just going to house rule them back in. <br /> <br /> There are communities of people that like different tribes, and some of them are going to wake up one day and find out their favorite are the bad guys now. If it\u2019s handled poorly, that\u2019ll be a sad day indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T02:03:41-07:00","id":1464480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464467#post1464467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna say it and I don't care if people will not understand: I want some of the get of fenris in my chronicles ALSO to be' some kind of fascist. Yes. I said it. I don't even care..</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be dumb because the Get of Fenris are allied in a multi-ethnic federation that spans the globe.<br /> <br /> Also, they already established the Get of Fenris hate Nazis so much they murdered an entire camp of them. Unless you plan to ignore that because you want fascist Get, then they made their opinion abundantly clear.<br /> <br /> However many Garou they needed, racism and fascism was punishable by death. Probably the Russian and Polish Get went, &quot;Yeah, no Nazis.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T02:28:38-07:00","id":1464485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464480#post1464480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it would be dumb because the Get of Fenris are allied in a multi-ethnic federation that spans the globe.<br /> <br /> Also, they already established the Get of Fenris hate Nazis so much they murdered an entire camp of them. Unless you plan to ignore that because you want fascist Get, then they made their opinion abundantly clear.<br /> <br /> However many Garou they needed, racism and fascism was punishable by death. Probably the Russian and Polish Get went, &amp;quot;Yeah, no Nazis.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Im totally ok with garou killing nazist garou. Nazism lead to wyrm taint. Its clear.<br /> <br /> But I think that a fascist like or cripto fascist fenris faction would be' extremely realistic in a modern day setting. Radicalization is easy for garou, and fenris ways of life speak clearly. I'm not against it. <br /> It's one of the main tragedy of werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-1