div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464747#post1464747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, why bother using the Union at all if you're going to change them so much?<br /> <br /> The whole point of the union is they're the Men in Black, shadowy conspiracy that suppresses the cure for cancer if it's not on the time table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey man, that was white wolfs perspective in Revised. Not mine. Plus considering they've been wiping their arse with the lore for 2 years now (quilted soft retcon type but still) .....<br /> <br /> Oh and the Seers of the Throne are boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-21-2021, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T09:56:49-07:00","id":1464761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464760#post1464760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey man, that was white wolfs perspective in Revised. Not mine. Plus considering they've been wiping their arse with the lore for 2 years now (quilted soft retcon type but still) .....<br /> <br /> Oh and the Seers of the Throne are boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Conceded.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T11:56:44-07:00","id":1464784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464746#post1464746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In union revised the union conceded they didn't rule the world, they're just the group with the most clout so they don't really 'control' any of those things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even earlier, it started becoming fact with the original Convention books, and it was pretty much fully canonized with the old Guide to the Technocracy (a brilliant book). The Technocracy is rich and influential and can get away with a lot, but thy don't control the world. Just like the Vampires don', no matter how they delude themselves. Late Revised and M20 pushed this even further with them realising that they may be losing at the same rate as the Traditions due to issues with the consensus and their own internal clusterfucks.<br /> <br /> And the whole &quot;cure for cancer isn't on the timetable&quot;? It's more humanity's fault, than theirs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T12:22:44-07:00","id":1464786,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure you can entirely lay the blame on humanity there. Something I think Revised got right, however much it might not have been great for just playing the game, is what it dubbed Apathy.<br /> <br /> One of the Union's greatest flaws is thinking that with enough control and power they can overwhelm human psychology, rather than trying to work with human nature to get results. This is a neat and convenient, but still appropriate, condensation of what fuels anti-intellectualism. And the human propensity for anti-intellectualism is the root of Apathy. The Time Table is, in many ways, as flawed as economic models that treat humans as well informed rational actors. The Union's failure to account for how humans actually work, instead of just churning out things as if humans worked the way the Technocrats want them to work poisoned their own well; making it much much harder to for the Union to deliver its idealistic promises to humanity while still taking the power they say they need to get it done, and the vicious cycle that ensued.<br /> <br /> So, yes, a &quot;cure for cancer,&quot; isn't on the Time Table because humanity isn't letting it be. But humanity isn't letting it be because of an instinctual response to how the Time Table has been implement as well.<br /> <br /> Hell, I could probably write a pretty large rant about how &quot;cure for cancer&quot; as a phrase particularly epitomizess the way this works (though the tl;dr version: there's no cure for cancer, because there's no &quot;cancer&quot; there's hundreds of cancers that vary wildly in how much a cure can ever be a realistic possibility).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T14:14:43-07:00","id":1464791,"title":"","content":"Oh I agree. The issue is more complex than just Humans being idiots or Technocracy having jaded assholes who have settled for less in Charge while fundamentally being a utopian project. I may have slightly over corrected as the whole Technocray are evil fascists making the world horrible is a relic of 1E Mage that we've supposed to have outgrown by now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T15:55:43-07:00","id":1464804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464710#post1464710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it depends on how separated from their human host societies you believe a tribe is. For, your points are all valid. For my taste, however, I feel that somewhere in the Dark Ages the number of homids started to grow and lupus born stated to decline and with that, the the rise of lost cubs within any tribe, the garou became more than just members of their tribe, as part of their regular identity or sense of self. Which, in itself, might be a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wolf declines on that order didn't happen until about the 16th or 17th century, which is squarely going from the late Renaissance to the early industrial period. Also, Lost Cubs aren't going to end up being that influential in Garou society as a matter of course, and most Garou have a big shakeup after meeting spirits, possibly including ancestral spirits that they have personal connections to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T09:43:16-07:00","id":1464880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1463869#post1463869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if the retcon Metis out of the game. If they say, there haven't been new Metis born since the year 2000 or so, the Metis would be removed as a PC option and that is okay.<br /> If the go the &quot;Children of Osiris&quot; way - and each metis is turned into a homid or lupus breed by Luna, because she is crazy, that's fine, too....</div> </div> </div> </div>10 grand says the perfect M\u00e9tis sacrificed themselves so that children of two garou wouldn\u2019t be deformed and sterile anymore<br /> <br /> In other words : Jesus crinos superstar","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 10-22-2021, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T15:30:29-07:00","id":1464918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464880#post1464880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 10 grand says the perfect M\u00e9tis sacrificed themselves so that children of two garou wouldn\u2019t be deformed and sterile anymore</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no accent marks on metis, it is pronounced mee-teez and not may-tee.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In other words : Jesus crinos superstar </div> </div> </div>&quot;I will drink your cup of silver!...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T20:43:06-07:00","id":1464961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1463839#post1463839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, it sounded good until the Umbra thing (urgh.) As for the metis, I need to be honest they were going to be cut anyway. Metis as a concept is rife with ableism and child abuse, stuff that no longer flies as easily as it did when 1e was released.<br /> <br /> The removal of Garou shall not Mate with Garou, though, makes me a bit worried. In Forsaken, that made sense, since uratha are very much a disperate people. But garou are more structured.<br /> <br /> Has there been anything about the lupus breed?<br /> <br /> In general, it sounds like Forsaken a bit too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, how is it that the idea of a disabled person being a warrior of Gaia is ableism? In character most Garou definitely are, but this is just recognizing a problem we face instead of pretending we are not discriminated against.<br /> <br /> Getting rid of Metis is the most ableist decision I saw.<br /> <br /> I personally think that Garou mating with Garou would had made sense to begin with, but not now. If it was that way since always it would explain a lot better how isolationist Garou culture is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T23:22:25-07:00","id":1464974,"title":"","content":"The problem with ableism and the Garou-born is a very long tradition of linking disabilities to sin and divine punishment. WtA has, since formulating the as the products of a spiritual wrong coupling, positioned the game to be in line with thousands of years of justifying discrimination against people with disabilities due to the idea that it only happens because of spiritual misdeeds.<br /> <br /> WtA is not empowering towards disabilities, but derogatory. The Garou culture is of course also bigoted (which was a conscious choice by the creators), but the game never states an alternative idea of why the Garou-born are always deformed in some fashion. It always comes down to, &quot;Garou on Garou mating is bad, and the Garou born bare the markings of that badness.&quot; No matter how much we know the disabilities are just medical issues that have no moral cause, there are lots of disabled people that have been stigmatized because of the long standing cultural myths around why disabilities happen.<br /> <br /> Obviously, like many issues regarding disabilities, even among people with them, there's a lot of debate over how to represent them.<br /> <br /> That said, I will restate something from the other thread (since if we continue this too far moderation on this is likely to come up again):<br /> <br /> You don't need the Garou-born to play a disabled werewolf. Emphasizing disabilities as part of reality for human and wolf born Garou is a net positive for good representation of people with disabilities in the game, rather than forcing one Breed to carry all of that representation on its own very loaded shoulders.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T04:29:41-07:00","id":1464997,"title":"","content":"To a degree this is true, but my problem is what you do once this is already a part of the game.<br /> <br /> Suddenly changing the Metis won't change the previous years. Instead it says that you don't have disabilities anymore because it isn't a sin anymore. You're saying a society got rid of its main disabled population by being forgiven of their sins.<br /> <br /> As a disabled person, that's how I feel with this decision, while I'm ok with Forsaken due to the reasons you pointed, but also because it wasn't a thing there to begin with.<br /> <br /> Metis are definitely a complex problem the game created for itself, but just getting rid of it after 30 years don't give closure, instead reminds me that we are still facing many forms of elimination to this day, everywhere.<br /> <br /> Just to contextualize, disabled people, especially the disabled from birth, still face selective abortion, murder as treatment on birth, killing by parents before turning 12, social pressure to suicide, treatment-as-correction in lieu of treatment as life improvement, targeted neutering, social isolation, just to cite the most common forms of elimination.<br /> <br /> It all happens at the every modern society, even the most economically developed ones, and indeed it is more effective among the richer social strata. What's more, with an alarming frequency news of those things happening portrays the offenders as tragic victims of their circumstances and the disabled victims as doomed to a life of suffering anyways, with a clear tone of &quot;it was for the best&quot;.<br /> <br /> When the game made Garou society be obviously wrong in their treatment of Metis and the modern elements arguing for better integration of them, it felt as recognition that we suffer this and it is wrong. And having Crinos as Breed form definitely feel as vindication. Why not start from there and change the idea that this is a sign of sin instead of changing that those people exist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T13:52:06-07:00","id":1465036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464997#post1464997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To a degree this is true, but my problem is what you do once this is already a part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, though I am firmly in the camp of keep the Garou-born, but fix them. I'm just not convinced that keeping them is better than not-fixing them (since, as noted, you can deal with disabilities in the game without tying them to a specific splat, which would comfort a lot of people with disabilities that feel diminished instead of empowered by the current status quo).<br /> <br /> One suggestion I've made in the past that minimizes the erasure issue while addressing the &quot;disabilities are the product of sin&quot; issue: make it objectively the case that deformities are not the natural state of things. In the ancient ancient past, the Garou-born were like their counterparts in the Ajaba, Kitsune, and Nagah: elevated for their status as a bridge between the two halves of Garou nature. However, the other Garou got jealous of the imbalance in power, and after the crimes of the First Ronin, they used a grand punishment rite that forever scarred the Garou-born (and started the myth that the First Ronin and the First Garou-born were the same individual instead of being the first to suffer under this Garou imposed curse).<br /> <br /> The rest of Garou history doesn't particularly change, as Garou society hypocritically enshrines myth over fact (again). By early history, the common idea of how the Garou see the Garou-born is a cultural norm, but one we as the players know is false.<br /> <br /> This also creates the potential for stories as knowledge of the truth can be uncovered and what to do about it can be explored. Can it be undone? Do the Garou-born want it undone as its become part of their identity? How many Garou are willing to accept having been so wrong for so long about it, and are going to deflect change over with the war on the Wyrm at hand? Etc.<br /> <br /> You also make it a bit more clear that the relationship between the Garou and the spirits isn't healthy because the spirits (for whatever reason) enabled this to continue for countless generations;; and continue to do so. Another overt reminder that the Garou's whole claim to divine authority to justify their actions isn't as &quot;true&quot; as it can seem with how the books present the setting; if the Garou can set the rules they live by, it's not Gaia that's inherently guiding their path..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T22:26:47-07:00","id":1465097,"title":"","content":"That would be an interesting solution, especially when it includes the question of wanting or not to change this part of your own identity, as it is a hot topic among the disabled community.<br /> <br /> Another one I thought was that it could have been originally a kind of blessing to the community, as the disabilities make the individual a source of new outlooks on unexpected things, but pride alone made the Garou reject the idea and change a command that already existed but didn't meant that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T01:30:36-07:00","id":1465105,"title":"","content":"The name needs to change. But other than that, I like the metis. Maybe in modern times the stigma won't be so bad, but curing them is... a poor resolution. <br /> <br /> 1- If the Garou could just have garanteed healthy and unstigmatized garou by fucking eachother, Kinfolk would lose a lot of their value and the garou would become much more insular, perhaps to the point where they've got nothing in common with humanity. <br /> <br /> 2 Unless two Garou breeding was changed so that the child didn't always breed true (obtaining a Wolf of man, depending on the mother's breed?) or it became really hard to concieve, The Garou have basically fixed their &quot;we can win battles but we lose wars&quot; status. I mean they can now potentially increase their numbers by up to 50% each year with metis births alone with an 8 year wait on returns (realistically, perhaps the Garou would only achieve a 20% increase, but even a 10% increase from just metis is gamechanging; this is an explosive and compoundable growth rate. <br /> <br /> 3: Garou society isn't meant to be <i>nice. </i>you're people with power, enabled by religion to do whatever you like for some nebulous greater good, frequently exposed to extreme violence and traumatic situations. Thats a recipe for monsters and dysfunction. Not to mention that Garou have an imbuilt &quot;override consent&quot; power for godsake. It's a grand recipe for <i>fucked up</i>. Don't sugar coat it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T01:56:39-07:00","id":1465107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1465105#post1465105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- If the Garou could just have garanteed healthy and unstigmatized garou by fucking eachother, Kinfolk would lose a lot of their value and the garou would become much more insular, perhaps to the point where they've got nothing in common with humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, and I would find that a bad thing. And kind of a different way as W20, where basically kinfok and pre-change garou are not distinguishable from each other and basically any kinfolk could be a late-change garou.<br /> <br /> But, if the garou society (re-)discovers that the deformities of the garou-born are a curse layed upon them by the garou society, it doesn't mean that the curse is revokable, meaning, their status might change, but the game itself doesn't too much.<br /> If they are cured by divine interventions, then too, the game will change, but more drastically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1465105#post1465105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 Unless two Garou breeding was changed so that the child didn't always breed true (obtaining a Wolf of man, depending on the mother's breed?) or it became really hard to concieve, The Garou have basically fixed their &quot;we can win battles but we lose wars&quot; status. I mean they can now potentially increase their numbers by up to 50% each year with metis births alone with an 8 year wait on returns (realistically, perhaps the Garou would only achieve a 20% increase, but even a 10% increase from just metis is gamechanging; this is an explosive and compoundable growth rate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'd say W5 developers are aware of that. If they really want to abolish &quot;garou shall not breed with garou&quot;, they will change the mechanics drastically. And, my guess is, it will be metaplot, not retcon. If it is done to my satisfaction, I doubt, but I see that there are other players with other need. Personally, I would like a change where there is more than one possible explanation so STs and players can choose how the change came into the game world....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1465105#post1465105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3: Garou society isn't meant to be <i>nice. </i>you're people with power, enabled by religion to do whatever you like for some nebulous greater good, frequently exposed to extreme violence and traumatic situations. Thats a recipe for monsters and dysfunction. Not to mention that Garou have an imbuilt &quot;override consent&quot; power for godsake. It's a grand recipe for <i>fucked up</i>. Don't sugar coat it.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but apparently the things that a game can, can't, should and shouldn't do have changed since 1st Edition, even since revised and W20. I would like to have the game still reflect the problems of garou society and possibly make it harder to play an all out nice guy, by possibly forcing some negative character traits onto all characters at creation, but well will have to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T02:20:09-07:00","id":1465110,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, it's worth remembering that these are games, meant to be enjoyed as they're played.<br /> <br /> It is much easier to have a &quot;muted&quot; central game where things might feel sugar coated to some for the people that don't want to deal with real life shit they have to put up with, You can always add dark elements to layer in for people that want it much more easily than the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T07:20:30-07:00","id":1465134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1465105#post1465105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The name needs to change. But other than that, I like the metis. Maybe in modern times the stigma won't be so bad, but curing them is... a poor resolution.<br /> <br /> 1- If the Garou could just have garanteed healthy and unstigmatized garou by fucking eachother, Kinfolk would lose a lot of their value and the garou would become much more insular, perhaps to the point where they've got nothing in common with humanity.<br /> <br /> 2 Unless two Garou breeding was changed so that the child didn't always breed true (obtaining a Wolf of man, depending on the mother's breed?) or it became really hard to concieve, The Garou have basically fixed their &quot;we can win battles but we lose wars&quot; status. I mean they can now potentially increase their numbers by up to 50% each year with metis births alone with an 8 year wait on returns (realistically, perhaps the Garou would only achieve a 20% increase, but even a 10% increase from just metis is gamechanging; this is an explosive and compoundable growth rate.<br /> <br /> 3: Garou society isn't meant to be <i>nice. </i>you're people with power, enabled by religion to do whatever you like for some nebulous greater good, frequently exposed to extreme violence and traumatic situations. Thats a recipe for monsters and dysfunction. Not to mention that Garou have an imbuilt &quot;override consent&quot; power for godsake. It's a grand recipe for <i>fucked up</i>. Don't sugar coat it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The name doesn't worries me so much because it makes sense from the perspective that it is how a bigoted society call them, but at this point proposals for change should be a thing, with the game letting in the air if the old term is still standard use or an artifact only found in writing and the mouths of really bigoted people.<br /> <br /> 1- being honest I already find that the Garou society is that insular, it doesn't strikes me as the product of a people that grew up among humans or wolves before coming to the fold. And even the Crinos born need Kinfolk caretakers before their First Change, or each birth would remove the parents from the war for too long a time and have a very high mortality rate for the children.<br /> <br /> 2- I don't worry with game change. This is the After Judgement edition, my problem with V5 is less that they changed things and more that they were too shy doing it (and bad writing all over the place). A Nation that isn't facing this particular problem anymore is ok to me, and even helps to deliver the notion that the Apocalypse came and went and the prophecy was fulfilled that all Garou meant to be there were already born by the end of the 90's.<br /> <br /> 3- I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, though, with one caveat: it is definitely possible to be so sugar coated as to be just as offensive or worse than not being so, and that's a big risk when they get rid of Metis entirely. There is also the responsibility of the game as social criticism, and this is a stated goal for WoD instead of a theoretical argument. Once you assume this responsibility, the fact that some people may take you seriously solidifies it.<br /> <br /> But yeah, at the same time no one should feel forced to deal with themes they don't feel comfortable with, and some may not feel like it precisely because they already deal with it as victims IRL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T10:25:38-07:00","id":1465156,"title":"","content":"You don't like metis<br /> Play a homid.<br /> or ask your ST if they can compromise<br /> <br /> Just taking out anything potentially upsetting and you might as well take out violence or the notion that climate change is real. I don't want the whole game coddled because someone had the vague impression that it relates to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T10:41:14-07:00","id":1465164,"title":"","content":"I think just not detailing how widespread is the prejudice is a good compromise. Groups that want to explore it can apply it as broadly as they want, groups that don't just reserve it for especially jerk ish characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T15:23:43-07:00","id":1465192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1465156#post1465156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't like metis<br /> Play a homid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lupus is the superior breed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T15:26:08-07:00","id":1465193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1465164#post1465164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think just not detailing how widespread is the prejudice is a good compromise. Groups that want to explore it can apply it as broadly as they want, groups that don't just reserve it for especially jerk ish characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't things like that in prior editions? There's not things, like, a ritual to punish metis for being metis... Or a chart saying how many % of the NPCS will mistreat the metis PC...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T16:40:06-07:00","id":1465208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1465192#post1465192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lupus is the superior breed</div> </div> </div> </div> Wouldn't suprise me if they're up for the chop as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T16:49:29-07:00","id":1465210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1465193#post1465193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't things like that in prior editions? There's not things, like, a ritual to punish metis for being metis... Or a chart saying how many % of the NPCS will mistreat the metis PC...</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone calls them Metis and no one questions it. This is not High Tongue or a heavenly mandate, it is a cultural decision to use one of the most offensive words available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T19:50:24-07:00","id":1465463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464467#post1464467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't. <br /> <br /> I'm gonna say it and I don't care if people will not understand: I want some of the get of fenris in my chronicles ALSO to be' some kind of fascist. Yes. I said it. I don't even care. <br /> What do we expect from a might is right tribe which is seeying her mother dying and every way they tried to save her , failing? We seriously expect to see them, all of them, moderate and not problematic? Oh come one. <br /> Ethnic tension, social tension, rampant pollution, global warming. This game is supposed to be' adult. We got genocidal red talons, terrorist Bond gnawers, abusive fianna, and vaguely fascist fenris is offensive ? Why ? Where is the maturity here ?<br /> I despise the nazi. A lot. And I despise the fascists. That doesnt mean that removing a realistic faction of the get will solve my problem with them. White wolf took distance from this shit many times. But this is an adult game, always has been, and basically every person I know like it because with every tribe comes some kind of problem within their tribal nature. Every tribe has some kind of internal internal conflict. Progress vs tradition. When they refuse to embrace adaptation they fail. When they forget or forsake tradition, they lost themselves. When they radicalize themselves, something bad happen. <br /> To have a well done and well depicted Extreme faction is not a way to exclude people or to offend someone. On the countrary, its a good way to face, to truly face problems. Fenris ways, even if moderate can be' seen as fascist in many ways. <br /> A character who is raised by an aryan brotherhood like pack and now sees the truth on the world, rediming himself , a story of deep redemption and pain.<br /> A character who is the grandson of an ss soldier and now is facing mistrust by other garou just because his bloodline. <br /> A bigot fenrir who is saved by a non binary garou or a masculinity-speecher who is in fact gay. <br /> I only see interesting stories coming out from the Extreme faction of every tribe. I see complications. I see very human antagonists and even very tragic protagonists in stories of redemption and sacrifice. <br /> <br /> Nobody wants fascist gamers at their table. But I want stories to tell. Rough, dirty, dangerous stories and honestly I dont fear to be' judged because of my creativity and my Players ability to Play a mature game where mature stuff happens, where dangerous characters can pop up.<br /> I like my werewolf game problematic and ambiguous when it comes to morality, justice, nature , anger , hate, war and social justice. <br /> To force player to Play fascist character or to say &amp;quot;this tribe is fascist&amp;quot; would be' of course extremely unjust, attract wrong people at the table and so on. And I'm not saying this. <br /> And I'm not against a moderate offshot. Im against the removal of an important tribe, the one that makes you think the most about that part of anger and solutions that bring you straight to intolerance. My feeling here is that the tribe would be' removed not because it's a fascist tribe (which is not) but just because the fenris have &amp;quot;porblematic &amp;quot; point of views. Which is just stupid and immature. <br /> <br /> But better to have the fenris removed than totally warped I suppose. Sadly.<br /> Pure Marketing ? Probably .<br /> I hope this message is clear enough because people seems to like to misunderstand this kind of things just to feel morally superior. <br /> <br /> Sorry for my poor english.</div> </div> </div> </div>100% agree (especially the Nazi's part). They say that people who forgot their history are doomed to repeat it. And remember, we are the storytellers. My grandma told me a few times about few decent soldiers in german army during the IIww. My grandpa said once, that even if he hates what they did he respect them as enemies (he was a polish soldier).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T20:09:46-07:00","id":1465465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch?p=1464632#post1464632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm from Poland and true , todays political scene is a fucking mess. If I could I would remove them all ( politics) from political scene one by one through some garou nasty punishing rite cause the truth is that every one of them would not bear the consequences of their actions.<br /> <br /> Polish Fenrir? My God, in popular fantasy magazine there was Rage across the Poland. And Get was represented by polish football fans, shit that was weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, I remember that. I somewhere got part of this setting. It wasn't so bad. After all I remember Dunsirn hooligan from Aberdeen from Giovanni CB, or ex-Celtic junior team coach permanently banned from football for using violence (also Dunsirn) from Ready Made characters for V20. Also Fianna were described as sport fans so polish Gets as football fans is ok for me. One of my friends used to play a hooligan and it was one of the best display of character concept I ever saw. As for polish politics I agree with you. I got an idea: let's form a party and call it IDK Impergium \ud83d\ude09?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T21:41:16-07:00","id":1465475,"title":"","content":"I don't even like the idea of the Red Talons becoming unplayable. <br /> <br /> Yes, they're one of the least played tribes by far. <br /> Yes, few people play them well<br /> <br /> But like malkavians, who attract the fools to the point that almost everyone plays them shit, the people who play Malkavian/Red Talon well play them <i>really well</i>. A Tribe that rejects and hates its own humanity is just fascinating RP material. <br /> <br /> They're also quite lacking in the combat gifts department, so you can rarely win with might, you must win with cunning. <br /> <br /> If you're going to get rid of the Talons, you might as well get rid of the Malks, because lots of malk players are stupid toxic shitbags and you'll have to filter out a lot of shit before you can find a diamond. Talons are the same, only differing in that they're 1 of 13 almost equally playable tribes rather than 1/7 almost equally playable OG camarilla clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsSc